IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 92 to 94 -- WHO ADMINISTERS THE ACT.
-- Piece cp6, lines 2638 to 2651 of the Act file.
--
-- Section 92 divides the administration: the Minister (of Employment and Social Development, section 91) has the control and
-- direction of everything except Part I; the Minister of National Revenue has Part I and must report to the Minister the
-- information the Minister needs; and may make available a report for policy analysis, research or evaluation. Sections 93 and 94
-- oblige two departments to give the assistance the Governor in Council directs.
--
-- These provisions address officials only. They are encoded for what they decide (which Minister holds a Part; what information
-- passes from one Minister to the other; which department must assist when directed) and not as machinery, because the passage of a
-- person's earnings information from the tax authority to the Minister is how the Record of Earnings (section 95) is filled.
-- The seat asks them only as "who deals with what, and who sees my information".
--
-- THE JURAL RELATIONS: the Minister of National Revenue's duty to report, with no holder of the claim named in the text (the Minister
-- who needs the information is the natural holder); the Minister of National Revenue's liberty to make a report available, and
-- the contributor's no-right that other law would otherwise give against it ("despite any other Act or law"); the two departments'
-- duties to assist, owed to the Minister, when directed.

§ `Part III -- administration of the Act (sections 92 to 94)`

§§ `Section 92 -- control and direction of the administration`

-- src:2639 | Administration of Act
-- src:2640 | 92 (1) The Minister has the control and direction of the administration of this Act other than Part I.
@ref Act s 92(1) (src:2639-2640)
DECLARE `cp6 Part of the Act for its administration` IS ONE OF
    `Part I of the Act`
    `a Part of the Act other than Part I`

@ref Act s 92(1), (2) (src:2639-2642)
GIVEN part IS A `cp6 Part of the Act for its administration`
GIVETH A Minister
`s 92 — the Minister with control and direction of the administration of the part` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    -- subsection (2): the Minister of National Revenue has control and direction of the administration of Part I
    WHEN `Part I of the Act` THEN `the Minister of National Revenue`
    -- subsection (1): the Minister (section 91) has it for "this Act other than Part I"
    WHEN `a Part of the Act other than Part I` THEN `the Minister of Employment and Social Development`

-- src:2641 | Duties of Minister of National Revenue
-- src:2642 | (2) The Minister of National Revenue has the control and direction of the administration of Part I and shall from time to time each year report to the Minister
-- src:2643 | (a) such information obtained under this Act with respect to the earnings and contributions of any contributor as is required by the Minister to permit the calculation of the amount of the unadjusted pensionable earnings to be shown to the account of the contributor in the Record of Earnings established under section 95, and to identify in the Record of Earnings the unadjusted pensionable earnings of contributors, according to information contained in returns made pursuant to Part I;
-- src:2644 | (b) such information obtained with respect to the earnings of any person as is required by the Minister to permit the determination of the amount of any benefit that may be payable under this Act to or in respect of that person or of the amount of any benefit that may be payable to or in respect of that person by reason of which any financial adjustment may be required to be made pursuant to any agreement entered into under subsection 80(1); and
-- src:2645 | (c) such statistical and other general information as is necessary for the administration of this Act including the conduct of actuarial and other studies relating to the operation of this Act.
@ref Act s 92(2) (src:2641-2645)
DECLARE `cp6 Kind of information the Minister of National Revenue reports to the Minister` IS ONE OF
    `earnings and contributions information needed for the Record of Earnings`
    `earnings information needed to determine a benefit or a financial adjustment`
    `statistical and other general information necessary for the administration of the Act`
    `information of another kind`

@ref Act s 92(2) (src:2641-2645)
GIVEN kind IS A `cp6 Kind of information the Minister of National Revenue reports to the Minister`
      `the information was obtained under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister requires the information for the purpose the paragraph describes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is necessary for the administration of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(2) — the Minister of National Revenue must report the information to the Minister` kind `the information was obtained under this Act` `the Minister requires the information for the purpose the paragraph describes` `the information is necessary for the administration of this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    -- (a) "such information obtained under this Act ... as is required by the Minister to permit the calculation of the amount of
    -- the unadjusted pensionable earnings to be shown to the account of the contributor in the Record of Earnings ..."
    WHEN `earnings and contributions information needed for the Record of Earnings` THEN
        `the information was obtained under this Act` AND `the Minister requires the information for the purpose the paragraph describes`
    -- (b) "such information obtained with respect to the earnings of any person as is required by the Minister to permit the
    -- determination of the amount of any benefit ... or ... any financial adjustment"
    WHEN `earnings information needed to determine a benefit or a financial adjustment` THEN
        `the information was obtained under this Act` AND `the Minister requires the information for the purpose the paragraph describes`
    -- (c) "such statistical and other general information as is necessary for the administration of this Act including the
    -- conduct of actuarial and other studies"
    WHEN `statistical and other general information necessary for the administration of the Act` THEN
        `the information is necessary for the administration of this Act`
    WHEN `information of another kind` THEN FALSE

-- src:2646 | Information provided by Minister of National Revenue
-- src:2647 | (3) Despite any other Act or law, the Minister of National Revenue or any person that he or she designates may make available to the Minister a report providing information that is necessary for the purpose of policy analysis, research or evaluation related to the administration of this Act.
@ref Act s 92(3) (src:2646-2647)
GIVEN `the report is made available by the Minister of National Revenue or a person that Minister designates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report provides information that is necessary for policy analysis, research or evaluation related to the administration of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 92(3) — the report may be made available to the Minister despite any other Act or law` `the report is made available by the Minister of National Revenue or a person that Minister designates` `the report provides information that is necessary for policy analysis, research or evaluation related to the administration of this Act` MEANS
    -- "Despite any other Act or law": no other Act or law is a condition, so none is an input.
        `the report is made available by the Minister of National Revenue or a person that Minister designates`
    AND `the report provides information that is necessary for policy analysis, research or evaluation related to the administration of this Act`

§§ `Sections 93 and 94 -- assistance in the administration`

-- src:2648 | Duty of Minister of Public Works and Government Services
-- src:2649 | 93 The Minister of Public Works and Government Services shall furnish the Minister with such assistance in the administration of this Act as the Governor in Council may direct.
@ref Act s 93 (src:2648-2649)
GIVEN `the Governor in Council has directed the Minister of Public Works and Government Services to furnish assistance of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 93 — the Minister of Public Works and Government Services must furnish the Minister with the assistance` `the Governor in Council has directed the Minister of Public Works and Government Services to furnish assistance of that kind` MEANS
    `the Governor in Council has directed the Minister of Public Works and Government Services to furnish assistance of that kind`

-- src:2650 | Duty of Canada Employment Insurance Commission
-- src:2651 | 94 The Canada Employment Insurance Commission shall furnish the Minister and the Minister of National Revenue with such assistance in the administration of this Act as the Governor in Council may direct.
@ref Act s 94 (src:2650-2651)
GIVEN `the Governor in Council has directed the Canada Employment Insurance Commission to furnish assistance of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 94 — the Canada Employment Insurance Commission must furnish the Minister and the Minister of National Revenue with the assistance` `the Governor in Council has directed the Canada Employment Insurance Commission to furnish assistance of that kind` MEANS
    `the Governor in Council has directed the Canada Employment Insurance Commission to furnish assistance of that kind`
